cd /workspace; D=grimoires/loa/a2a/audits/2026-10-21; cat > $D/SECURITY_ANALYSIS_TODO.md <<'EOF'
# Security analysis working file — sprint-1 audit (pr/head.diff, sprint-264) — 2026-10-21

| # | Kind | Location (head/) | Trust | Status | Note |
|---|------|------------------|-------|--------|------|
| 1 | source | evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh:258 `LOA_ABLATION_BATCH_CONTEXT` env | operator | PARTIAL | literal `1` only; guards a label (`eval_only`) not the capability (`oracle_open`) → MED-001 |
| 2 | source | evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh:242 `--suite-file` → `ARM_DEF.eval_only` | operator | PARTIAL | editable; no per-run provenance → MED-001 / LOW-003 |
| 3 | source | evals/harness/validate-suite.sh:87 `RULE_IDS` from took-effect.sh via sed | in-tree | SAFE | regex `^rule_([a-z_][a-z0-9_]*)()`; passed as argv, no shell re-eval |
| 4 | source | evals/harness/validate-suite.sh:157-180 suite arms (toggles, took_effect, eval_only) | operator | SAFE | type-exact, allowlisted; python3 -I |
| 5 | sink | evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh:341-345 jq config_edits (dry run, stdout only) | — | SAFE | jq data path; duplication only → MED-004 |
| 6 | sink | evals/harness/run-ablation.sh:1300-1301 trial exec with env prefix | — | SAFE | env set on the command only; arm ids regex-gated at :574 |
| 7 | sink | evals/tests/fixtures/ablation-pipeline-stub.sh:55 `>> $STUB_ENV_LOG` | test | N/A | test fixture |
| 8 | sink | evals/tests/pipeline-run.bats:1018 `yq load(strenv(SUITE_SRC))` | test | N/A | test fixture, in-tree path |
| 9 | flow | suite `priority` → run-ablation.sh:570 default plan | — | CONFIRMED | new arms absent → HIGH-001 |
| 10 | flow | components (report.py:1913) → primaries (:653) → compare (:732) → decide (:846) | — | CONFIRMED | pass-rate pair never forms for review-catch-only arms → HIGH-002 |
| 11 | flow | pipeline-run.sh REFUSAL (:244-252) vs eval_only exit (:259) ordering | — | CONFIRMED | eval_only pre-empts applicability refusal → LOW-004 |

Deferred (outside diff / not in workspace): lib/sandbox-mount.sh apply_arm_toggles, took-effect.sh rule bodies, ablation-grade.sh, gen-fixtures.py, grimoires/loa/evals/ablation-2.0 suite root.
EOF
cat > $D/findings.jsonl <<'EOF'
{"id":"ARCH-001","category":"architecture","criterion":"integration","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/suites/ablation-2.0.yaml","line":55,"code_snippet":"priority: [a0_bare, a1_full, a2_no_sprint_plan, a3_one_voice, a4_no_gates, a7_effort_medium, a5_no_flatline, a6_one_window]","finding":"The four cycle-131 arms are not in priority; run-ablation.sh derives the default arm set from priority (run-ablation.sh:570-571), so a default batch never schedules them.","reasoning_trace":"Read suite header (line 12 names priority as a run-ablation.sh input) -> run-ablation.sh usage :24-25 and jq at :570-571 -> arms :98-105 absent from :55 -> AT-13 checks arm list only.","confidence":"high","remediation":"Append the four ids to priority and extend AT-13 to assert every non-absent arm is in priority.","reference":"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/684.html"}
{"id":"ARCH-002","category":"architecture","criterion":"correctness","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-report.py","line":653,"code_snippet":"if \"all\" in types or REVIEW in types: return list(pba.get(\"all_types\") or [PASS, CATCH])","finding":"Review-catch-only components receive hidden_test_pass_rate as a primary; compare() restricts it to BUILD_TYPES tasks (:732) so n==0, usable() false, nopair true in decide() (:846-887); remove/simplify unreachable.","reasoning_trace":"components filter :1913 admits a0_bare_fable/a1_review_only/a1_no_dissent -> primaries :653-658 -> compare :732 -> usable :577 -> decide :846-887 -> decidable :926 always false.","confidence":"high","remediation":"Add a review_only primary shape (catch rate only) in suite rules and primaries(); add a report test reaching remove/simplify for such an arm.","reference":"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1023.html"}
{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"MEDIUM","score":4,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":258,"code_snippet":"EVAL_ONLY=false; [[ \"$(jq -r '.eval_only // false' <<<\"$ARM_DEF\")\" == true ]] && EVAL_ONLY=true","finding":"The refusal guards the open mount via the eval_only label and an operator-settable env var, never via toggles.oracle_open; no batch-context provenance is recorded per run. Confirmed by cross-model review DISS-C-001.","reasoning_trace":"validate-suite.sh enforces oracle_open=>eval_only (:179-180) but pipeline-run.sh never runs it; arm-evidence records oracle_open/mount_overlay but not eval_only/batch_context.","confidence":"medium","remediation":"Refuse on toggles.oracle_open too; write eval_only and batch_context into meta/arm-evidence.txt.","reference":"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html"}
{"id":"ARCH-003","category":"architecture","criterion":"correctness","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-report.py","line":1913,"finding":"a0_bare_fable (a bare-model baseline per the suite comment) passes the components filter and gets a keep/remove row; k becomes 9 and the tests lock it in.","reasoning_trace":"suite :94-95 calls it A0 on the review model; code comment :1911-1912 excludes baselines; filter excludes only CONTROL/BARE/absent/eval_only.","confidence":"medium","remediation":"Exclude loa_mount:false arms (or a baseline flag) from components; set tests to 8.","reference":"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1023.html"}
{"id":"ARCH-004","category":"architecture","criterion":"completeness","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-report.py","line":2003,"code_snippet":"detail_arms = [BARE, CONTROL] + components","finding":"The eval_only arm appears neither in Decisions nor Per-arm detail; its open-mount A/B cannot be read from the report.","reasoning_trace":"detail_arms inherits the components exclusion; rows surface only at :1624.","confidence":"medium","remediation":"Add eval_only arms to detail_arms or render a decides-nothing comparison.","reference":"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/684.html"}
{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"duplication","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":341,"finding":"Dry-run config_edits jq re-implements the apply_arm_toggles key mapping by hand; tests pin the copy.","reasoning_trace":"lib/sandbox-mount.sh outside diff [ASSUMPTION it holds the mapping]; divergence would make the dry run lie.","confidence":"medium","remediation":"Expose the mapping from the library and call it.","reference":"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1041.html"}
{"id":"CQ-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"duplication","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/validate-suite.sh","line":137,"finding":"TOGGLE_VALUES duplicates the library toggle vocabulary while RULE_IDS is derived from took-effect.sh. Confirmed by review DISS-C-002 of the review phase.","reasoning_trace":"Compare :87 (derived) with :137-139 (listed).","confidence":"medium","remediation":"Derive the vocabulary from the library or add an equality test.","reference":"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1041.html"}
{"id":"DOC-001","category":"devops","criterion":"documentation","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"pr/PR.md","line":1,"finding":"PR title claims a suite root (bounds 50/40) and an image self-check that are not in the diff; no AC Verification section.","reasoning_trace":"grep head.diff for grimoires/loa/evals, image, self-check: only the pre-existing fixture copy in run-ablation.bats:1196.","confidence":"high","remediation":"Add the files or retitle; add an AC walkthrough.","reference":"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html"}
{"id":"DOC-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"comments","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/suites/ablation-2.0.yaml","line":29,"finding":"Header says every mounted review-catch arm runs the closed mount; a1_full_openmount does not.","reasoning_trace":"suite :29-31 vs :104.","confidence":"high","remediation":"Qualify the sentence.","reference":"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1116.html"}
{"id":"DOC-003","category":"code_quality","criterion":"comments","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/suites/ablation-2.0.yaml","line":117,"finding":"Comment says 6 components; report prints 9.","reasoning_trace":"suite :117 vs AR-12 :189.","confidence":"high","remediation":"Update or drop the number.","reference":"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1116.html"}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"integrity","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-report.py","line":1913,"finding":"Component exclusion trusts the suite eval_only flag and never cross-checks row evidence (oracle_open, mount_overlay). Confirmed by cross-model review DISS-C-002.","reasoning_trace":"oracle_reason :584-588 already reads row oracle_open; components does not.","confidence":"low","remediation":"Exclude or fail on arms whose review-catch rows carry oracle_open=true; print a provenance mismatch line.","reference":"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/345.html"}
{"id":"CQ-003","category":"code_quality","criterion":"control_flow","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":259,"finding":"The eval_only exit precedes the REFUSAL handling (:318, :468-472), so a non-applicable eval_only arm outside the batch gets the eval_only message and no refusal record.","reasoning_trace":"REFUSAL computed :244-252, eval_only exit :259-262, REFUSAL acted on :318/:468.","confidence":"medium","remediation":"Act on REFUSAL first or fold eval_only into the REFUSAL chain.","reference":"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/684.html"}
{"type":"summary","sprint_id":"sprint-1","date":"2026-10-21","verdict":"CHANGES_REQUIRED","counts":{"critical":0,"high":2,"medium":6,"low":4},"excluded":0,"excluded_confirmed":0,"dissent":{"status":"clean","voices_succeeded":2,"advisory":2,"rejected":0,"degraded":false},"scope_limits":["lib/sandbox-mount.sh","took-effect.sh","ablation-grade.sh","gen-fixtures.py","suite root grimoires/loa/evals/ablation-2.0","bats suites not executed"]}
EOF
